1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,666
Welcome to ACME Bank —

2
00:00:01,666 --> 00:00:05,299
a fully working digital bank built with Next.js,

3
00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:10,296
React and Supabase. The public site even lists every fee up front.

4
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:13,928
Customers sign in with email and password.

5
00:00:13,928 --> 00:00:18,235
For the demo, this panel fills in one of six seeded customers.

6
00:00:18,937 --> 00:00:22,489
Olivia's overview shows her total and available balance,

7
00:00:22,489 --> 00:00:25,534
a sixty-day balance chart, spending by category,

8
00:00:25,534 --> 00:00:26,929
and upcoming payments.

9
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:32,433
In Accounts, two months of transactions can be searched and filtered

10
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:35,464
by account, status, type, category or date.

11
00:00:36,168 --> 00:00:38,950
Each account keeps a double-entry ledger,

12
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:41,867
with debits, credits and a running balance,

13
00:00:41,867 --> 00:00:43,224
all stored in cents.

14
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:46,237
Sending money takes three steps.

15
00:00:46,237 --> 00:00:49,117
Before she confirms, ACME shows the fee,

16
00:00:49,117 --> 00:00:52,069
the total and when the money will arrive.

17
00:00:52,783 --> 00:00:56,334
On the Cards page, she can lock her card instantly,

18
00:00:56,334 --> 00:00:58,423
or adjust limits and controls.

19
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:02,526
Statements are available for any period,

20
00:01:02,526 --> 00:01:03,714
as PDF or CSV.

21
00:01:04,427 --> 00:01:08,867
Support tickets keep the whole conversation with the bank's team in one thread.

22
00:01:09,582 --> 00:01:13,830
On a phone, the side menu turns into a bottom navigation bar.

23
00:01:14,583 --> 00:01:16,681
Staff get their own workspace.

24
00:01:16,681 --> 00:01:19,478
The operations overview tracks deposits,

25
00:01:19,478 --> 00:01:22,695
pending settlements, reviews and open tickets.

26
00:01:23,401 --> 00:01:28,249
Large transfers wait in the review queue until someone approves or rejects them.

27
00:01:28,954 --> 00:01:32,889
Admins drive the simulation: trigger scenarios like a fraud alert,

28
00:01:32,889 --> 00:01:36,466
and move the bank clock forward to settle pending transfers.

29
00:01:37,179 --> 00:01:39,723
Every action is recorded in the event log,

30
00:01:39,723 --> 00:01:42,267
and everything stays saved after a reload.

31
00:01:42,972 --> 00:01:45,987
That's ACME Bank: accounts, transfers,

32
00:01:45,987 --> 00:01:49,716
cards, statements and operations, in one place.
